sandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-07T09:49:38Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T09:52:20Z","body":"I'm not sure this is the appropriate way to handle this, and I'm not sure it makes sense to change code in this way to support hypothetical extensions using these. These RID owners are managed in specific ways by the server and I don't expect it is designed to allow random operation of them outside the designed use, when there are systems in place to create and handle the resources as is. This feels like it is either doing too much or too little without exposing other means to operate on the data, or controlling access to enforce expectations and design constraints\r\n\r\nI think this needs a proposal to discuss alternative solutions and the demand for this","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4902445679/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4902756509","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121021#issuecomment-4902756509","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121021","id":4902756509,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJDognQ","user":{"login":"monokrome","id":242997,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0Mjk5Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/242997?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monokrome","html_url":"https://github.com/monokrome","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monokrome/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monokrome/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monokrome/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monokrome/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monokrome/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monokrome/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monokrome/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monokrome/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monokrome/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-07T10:25:26Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T10:27:03Z","body":"@AThousandShips Well, this is the first moving piece to get it moving for some use-cases although a better solution is surely to derive a reasonable abstraction and clean up the moving pieces. Its honestly wild that the current solution even exists as-is in production.\r\n\r\nThat said, if you wanted to go back to a more in-depth design phase then it'd have been nice to hear that before you made a big deal about my commit message and had me rebase/edit it. Always nice when people use \"respect other peoples' time\" as an excuse for \"I perceive my time as more valuable than yours\", though.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4902756509/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"h